# /etc/cerberus/config.yaml.example was a conffile up to and including 0.10.4.
# The template now ships at /usr/share/cerberus/config.yaml.example so upgrades
# always refresh it; dpkg will not drop a conffile on its own, so retire the old
# path explicitly. rm_conffile preserves the file (as .dpkg-bak) if the admin
# modified it, and is a no-op if they had already removed it.
#
# The version is 0.10.5~, NOT 0.10.4~. dpkg-maintscript-helper only acts when the
# version being upgraded FROM is older than or equal to this value, and 0.10.4~
# sorts *before* 0.10.4 -- so an upgrade from the very release that shipped the
# conffile would have skipped the removal entirely. 0.10.5~ sorts just below the
# release that drops it, covering 0.10.4 and everything earlier.
rm_conffile /etc/cerberus/config.yaml.example 0.10.5~ cerberus-api
